<title>HONG KONG: Shougang Tech interim net up 12.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Shougang Tech interim net up 12.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	  3.6    vs 3.2 (adjusted)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)   1.0    vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	 nil    vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			   15.09  vs 13.38</p>
<p>    Turnover		    338.05 vs 322.32</p>
<p>    Company name		Shougang Concord Technology Holdings</p>
<p>				    Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		 October 16-18</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	  October 31</p>
<p>NOTE - Shougang Concord Technology is a maker of telephones, power cords and plugs.</p>
<p>The company proposed a bonus issue of one 1999 warrant for every six shares, each bonus warrant will entitle the holder therof to subscribe for fully-paid new shares at the initial subscription price of HK$0.6, subject to adjustment, from the date of issue to December 31, 1998.</p>
<p>Comparative share earings has been adjusted for the rights issue.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
